needs an insurance agent you're going  after the people who are ideal clients  for you and you love working with and  you have shared shared passions with so  identifying first you know your unique  value proposition who is Joe the  insurance guy what do you do that's  different everybody else and then start  defining who  your customers are so I would try to be  as specific as you can with that you  obviously don't want to limit yourself  off and say you know only people who  like to clip in Indians and who are you  know 50 to 55 and men right there might  be a little specific but you want to do  try to define your target market as much  as you can with your customer base so  look at your age group look at look at  interest look at their stage in life  look at what some of their needs are and  build up a profile the ideal person that  you want to target and from there if you  can specialize in those people and you  go and you tell them when you're meeting  with them that you specialize with those  types of people and you can show how  you've helped people who are like them  the more like they don't want to sign up  with you instead of I'm Joe and I sell  insurance to anybody and everybody right  it's a lot harder to make that kind of  sale so you may be turning away business  that you can make some money from but  are not ideal clients and then focus on  the ones who are great potential clients  for you because you know you can service  your needs  from there once I can a clearly  explained why I'm different and I can  explain the type of customers that I  want to go after then you can start with  your marketing strategy  and for you I try to look at events to  start so it's a very personal business  if I'm gonna work with an insurance  agent I want to know that again he  understands my needs likes what I'm  about I can relate to him really well  and so events are great way to do that  you're meeting people again you know we  want to treat your finding events where  your target customers are hanging out at  so it's a great way to make those first  connections  I would then look to get in front of  connectors so potential referral  partners who can you partner up with  where you prefer them business they  queer for you business I look to get  into the local media you want to be seen  as the local expert for insurance for  you know whatever age group again  whoever your target customers are and  pitching the media is a lot easier when  you have your unique value proposition  and you know who you're targeting is  your customers and you have a story to  be able to tell instead of just I'm Joe  the sales guy right so getting the media  local media especially we can have some  kind of ongoing relationship if you're  writing a monthly column for example in  your local media could really help  I then think about creating content and  for here you'd want to be creating  articles and other types of content that  again are geared towards your target  customer educating them creating a  monthly newsletter that goes out that  you also post on your website so giving  them ongoing useful helpful content that  talks about where the right with their  stage of life that might be able to you  might be able to help them with and new  products or services that you're coming  out with that again could be able to  help them and then I'd also create video  and if somebody is meeting you in an  event or they heard about you through  the media or the read one of your  articles a great way to introduce  yourself again is through video  especially if you haven't met them yet  and it's coming to a connector or media  another source people again this is a  very personal business for you people  will make decisions really quickly based  on seeing you and hearing you so if you  create a quick video of yourself that  goes up on your website when people land  they're able to learn a little bit about  you kind of see what you like what  you're about again you're talking about  these two things your unique value  proposition and types of customers you  like to deal with and it goes a long way  to be able to make a warm welcome online  when you haven't actually met somebody  face-to-face and when I first started my  business my website is off my name so  seven Carl calm I kind of hid behind my  content and we did a lot of profiles the  famous entrepreneurs and people started  writing in asking about me and who I was  and eventually I started creating more  and more content and got into video as  well and people seem to really like the  videos and it's a great way of people to  kind of get to know me and I've have  people come up to me and feel like they  already know me because they watch other  videos and they've seen all of them and  they know our regular viewers and you  know I don't know them yet but it's  great to meet them so you can have the  same relationship where people can come  to your site quickly watch your intro  video see you're a nice guy see that you  understand their needs and your catering  just to them and they'll start forming a  relationship with you even though you  haven't really set a relationship with  them yet so they're more opportune more  likely to pick up the phone I want to  call you so hope that helps so again  come up be unique value proposition what  makes you different identify who your  target customers are in as much detail  as you can then start your marketing  strategy through events going after  connector  get into the media create a content  strategy and creating some video as well  Joe I hope that's useful if you guys  like the video please leave a comment  below and it also always appreciate it  when you want to leave a thumbs up for  the videos so thank you and we'll see  you on the next episode  [Music]  you

